Thus (6.43) and (6.47) imply:

\[\left\|u^{n+1}-u\right\|_{X}\leq\gamma K\left\|u-u^{n}\right\|_{X}^{2}\]

and since \(\alpha^{\prime}\gamma K\leq 1/2\) this yields

\[\left\|u^{n+1}-u\right\|_{X}\leq(1/2)\left\|u^{n}-u\right\|_{X}.\]

Hence \(u^{n+1}\) belongs to \(S(u;\alpha^{\prime})\) and these two inequalities show that the sequence \((u^{n})\) converges quadratically to \(u\).

Next, consider the scheme (6.42). Like above, we start with \(u^{0}\) in \(S(u;\alpha^{\prime\prime})\) for some \(\alpha^{\prime\prime}\leq\alpha^{\prime}\) that we shall specify subsequently. Then (6.42) determines a unique sequence \((u^{n})\) and similarly, we have:

\[u^{n+1}-u=[D_{u}F(\lambda,u^{0})]^{-1}\int_{0}^{1}[D_{u}F(\lambda,u^{n}+t(u-u^ {n}))-D_{u}F(\lambda,u^{0})]\cdot(u-u^{n})\,dt.\]

Hence assuming that \(u^{n}\) belongs also to \(S(u;\alpha^{\prime\prime})\) we derive:

\[\left\|u^{n+1}-u\right\|_{X} \leq\gamma K(\left\|u^{n}-u^{0}\right\|_{X}+\left\|u-u^{0}\right\| _{X})\left\|u^{n}-u\right\|_{X}\] \[\leq 3\alpha^{\prime\prime}\gamma K\left\|u^{n}-u\right\|_{X}.\]

Therefore, by choosing

\[\alpha^{\prime\prime}<1/(3\gamma K)\]

we find that \(u^{n+1}\) belongs to \(S(u;\alpha^{\prime\prime})\) and that the sequence \((u^{n})\) converges linearly to \(u\). 

Let us apply Theorem 6.3 to solve the familiar class of problems

(6.48) \[F(\lambda,u)\equiv u+TG(\lambda,u)=0\ \ \ \ \ \forall\lambda\in\Lambda,\]

where \(X\) and \(Y\) are two Banach spaces, \(\Lambda\) is a compact interval of \(\mathbb{R}\), \(T\in\mathcal{L}(Y;X)\) and \(G\) is a \(\mathcal{C}^{2}\)-mapping from \(\Lambda\times X\) into \(Y\) with \(D^{2}G\) bounded on all bounded subsets of \(\Lambda\times X\). This last property implies the Lipschitz condition (6.43). Therefore, if \(\lambda\to u(\lambda)\) is a branch of _nonsingular solutions_ of (6.48), Newton's method defines a locally (and quadratically) convergent algorithm:

(6.49) \[(I+TD_{u}G(\lambda,u^{n}))\cdot u^{n+1}=T[D_{u}G(\lambda,u^{n})\cdot u^{n}-G( \lambda,u^{n})].\]

Likewise, the variant (6.42) is also locally (but linearly) convergent:

(6.50) \[(I+TD_{u}G(\lambda,u^{0}))\cdot u^{n+1}=T[D_{u}G(\lambda,u^{0})\cdot u^{n}-G( \lambda,u^{n})].\]

As an example, consider the Navier-Stokes equations:

(6.51) \[\left\{\begin{aligned} -\,v\,d\,{\bf u}+\,\sum_{j=1}^{N}u_{j}( \partial{\bf u}/\partial x_{j})+\,{\bf grad}\,p&={\bf f},\\ &\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\
